
                              Boss-Nuke Docs 
                         BoSS-NuKE v1.0 written by
                                 Big Boss
                                 
Welcome to 'BossNuke' - the world's fastest nuker!  

Features:
 -Full CONFERENCE ACCOUNTING support for /X 3.x users!
 -Finds uploaders in less than 2 seconds!
 -Stackable command line options!
 -Up to 20 filenames at once!
 -'Speed' award and destroy modes for FAST hassle free operation!
 -Create files to prevent them being uploaded!
 -Configuration file to allow configurable set-up!
 -Can be set up to RESTRICT files rather than DELETE them in config file.
 -Password file can be set up for better security.
 -Online detailed docs to help those 'slow-to-learn' cosysops ;-)
 -Built for Speeeeed!
 -Now Sigma Seven!'s Dupe File Checker code installed in the Ulog.x section!
 

Installation:
 
Installing this is somewhat simple.  Just copy the files to the paths suggested
and all should go well.  
The archive contains the following files:
  BossNuke.x              
  BossNuke.prefs
  BossNuke.pw
  Ulog.x      <----- /X 2.34 or higher /X needed to run this file.
  BossNuke.doc
Copy BossNuke.x to doors:nuke/ (or path to where you want nuker to go).
Copy BossNuke.prefs to s:
IF you want to have users enter a password BEFORE entering nuke door, copy
  BossNuke.pw to s: - otherwise copy to doors:nuke/ for storage for future.
Copy Ulog.x to doors:nuke/
Copy BossNuke.doc to where ever you want!

Make sure that you have the UDLOG options turned on in your AmiExpress 
  configuration.  Without this it will not find downloaders.  May not find
  uploaders either depending on if you have ulog.x installed or not!

For AmiExpress 3.x:   2 icons are included in the archive.  One is nuke.info
  and the other is FILECHECK.info.  Edit the nuke.info and set the correct
  path to the BossNuke file.  Then copy this to 'doors:commands/bbscmd/'
 
  The other icon is called FILECHECK.info.  This icon must be not be
  renamed!  Move this to the 'bbs:commands/syscmd/' directory.  Edit the 
  path to make sure it is to where you copied the ulog.x file to.

For AmiExpress 2.x:  Edit the bbs:commands/bbs.cmd file and add to it:
*nuke        XS200doors:nuke/BossNuke.x
Next Edit bbs:commands/sys.cmd file and add to it:
FILECHECK    XM001doors:nuke/ulog.x
(name of the sys.cmd entry MUST be 'FILECHECK' or it will not be run at the
 correct time!)

Make sure you have the file 'paths' in each conference on your bbs that
  contains the full download paths with no spaces after them a carriage
  return after the last entry (standard set up of the paths file).

Now it is time to edit the BossNuke.prefs file in the s: directory.
  Included with the archive is a 'default' example of a prefs file.  Let's look
  at this file:
  
Conference_Accounting=N
File_Restriction=N
Size=>LAME< 
Size=>DUPE< 
Size=>FAKE< 
Size=RENAMED
Size= >OLD< 
Size=CORRUPT
Size=OFFLINE
Size=FOREIGN
Size=>INTRO<
Size=>MUSIC<
Comment=2x Credits Given!
Comment=3x Credits Given!
Comment=User Deleted!
Comment=Credits Taken!
Comment=Comment5
Comment=Comment6
Comment=Comment7
Comment=Comment8
Comment=Comment9
Comment=Comment10

These must be in this same order. 
Line 1: Conference_Accounting=N   
	Conference_Accounting=Y
 	-Y turns on the conference accounting options.. to be used only with
         amiexpress 3.0 or higher when the conference_accounting is turned
    	 on inside the access icons.
    	 
Line 2: File_Restriction=N
	File_Restriction=Y
	-This turns on or off the File Deletion or File Restriction routine.
	 If 'Y' is selected, then BossNuke will RESTRICT the nuked files from   	
	 being downloaded, but will not delete them when the delete file
	 option is selected in the nuke door.  If 'N' is selected, then the
	 file will be deleted and replaced with a 40 byte file saying 
	 'Nuked by BossNuke' or something like that..
	 
Line 3: Size=>LAME< 
	This is the 7 character or less byte size comments to be used.
Line 4-12 are same as line 3 and must be included!
Line 13: First of 10 File Descriptions to be entered under the nuked files.
         Only 54 Characters will be included.
Lines 14-22 are rest of required file descriptions.
Line 23: DupeCheck=Y
	 DupeCheck=N
         This turns on or off Sigma Seven!'s Dupefilechecker that checks for
         duplicate files in the upload directory after each upload.  If a 
         duplicate file is found then the upload is moved to the hold.
         
Once all this is done, the Installation is complete.  

Note:  The Ulog.x file is optional but HIGHLY recommended!
       This marks an upload each time it's sent up.  It will create a 
       series of files with the format of 'ulog.[node#]' in each conference.
       These files will NEVER exceed 3200 bytes each.  They will make the 
       search for the uploaders become almost INSTANTANEOUS.  Without these,
       'BossNuke' must search the UDLOGS which is not as fast.  However, even
       using the UDLOG to search the uploader, it still is rather quick.
       There will be one file per node per conference created.
       
       I have added Sigma Seven!'s Duplicate Filechecker routines to this
       aswell!  You can turn it on or off in the BossNuke.prefs file as
       shown above.  This will scan the file uploaded against all your dirx
       files and if there exists a duplicate, then the upload is moved to 
       the sysop's hold.  A great routine now that Bytemaster is not planning
       to include this option in /X.  

       
PassWord File:
 If you want a password to be required to enter the door you must copy the
 file 'bossnuke.pw' to the s: directory.  The format of this file is like so:
 Line1: Number of entries (users that will have passwords).
 Line2: First entry  format: NAME,PASSWORD
 If you have the file BOSSNUKE.PW in s: then no one not listed in this file
 can enter BOSSNUKE.  So, if you do NOT want to enter pw's to use the door,
 do NOT put this file in the s: directory!  You can use the example file
 included in this archive to understand the exact format of this file.




Operation:

BossNuke has a thorough built in help screen.  Just type 'nuke -h' and you
  will see the online docs.  They are pretty thorough but we shall explain
  some of the features here aswell.

Easiest way to use this is to type 'nuke' and to follow the instructions on
  the screen.  It will allow you to enter up to 20 files at one time.
 
Stackable Commands:
  You can enter the filename(s) on the amiexpress command line aswell like:
  'Nuke Filename'  or 'nuke filename1 filename2 filename3'
  Doing this will bypass the prompt to enter files inside the door and 
  immediately being the nuking process.

Creating Files to prevent fakes uploaded:
  Enter '-c' as your first filename.  'nuke -c' or type nuke, and when asked
  for the first filename enter '-c'.  Then it will ask you the filenames to
  create.  These files will be skipped when attempted to be uploaded.
  
Speed Destroy Mode:
  Speed Mode is a great feature.  It allows you to nuke a series of files 
  all automatically without any further interaction with the nuker.
  Type 'nuke filename1 filename2 filename3 [times credits to take]' example:
  'nuke dw-ship1.zip dw-ship2.zip 2' 
  The above example will take 2x credits.  
  Speed mode will do the following:
  -Nuke files and delete them.
  -Search uploader.
  -Take credits stated on command line and save the user's account.
  -Send Msg to user.
  -Update File directory with BYTE comment #1.
  -Go to next file.
  Speed mode will NOT return credits to dlers or use an extended description.
  
Speed Award Mode:
  This is identical to Speed Destroy Mode except it is award the uploader for
  an excellent upload rather than nuke credits.  Speed Award Mode will do the 
  same as destroy mode except it will not delete the file and it will not 
  update the file directory.  Award mode is entered by specifying a negative
  number for the [times credits].  Example:
  'nuke filename1 filename2 -2' gives 2x additional credits to the user that
  uploaded the file.
  
  Both speed modes can nuke up to 10 files in less than 1 minute including 
  all msg's sent and all directories updated etc..  really handy if you are
  in a hurry.
  
The rest of this should be pretty much self evident.  If you have any questions
I can be reached on the AmiExpress support bbs or Mirage if you can manage an
account there.  Remember to type 'nuke -h' for online help.  Good luck and
suggestions are welcome to improve this utility!

Big Boss

